Separately licensed data

The MIT grant above does not cover Grand Comics Database-derived data in
src/data/collectedEditionEvidence.js, scripts/data/collected-editions/gcd-check-inputs.json,
scripts/data/collected-editions/gcd-editions.json, or
scripts/data/collected-editions/gcd-fixtures/. Those files are adaptations of
Grand Comics Database data (https://www.comics.org/) licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
Their attribution, source records and modification notices accompany the data.

The MIT grant above also does not cover the Grand Comics Database-derived release
dates and credits in scripts/data/owner-gcd/issues.json,
scripts/data/owner-mappings/avengers-armageddon.json and
src/data/avengers_armageddon.json. Those files are adaptations of Grand Comics
Database data (https://www.comics.org/) licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
Adapted for this project: each record keeps only the series name, issue number,
on-sale date and the script and pencils credits of the issue, turned into a release
date and writer, penciler and cover artist credits. Cover images, prose and notes are
never recorded. The records file carries the attribution and each record's source
address and retrieval date, the mapping names the source address beside each field it
supplies, and the app credits the Grand Comics Database on each comic it supplies.
